<td id="A3.T10.3.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="A3.T10.3.4.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">52.48</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T10.3.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T10.3.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb ltx_border_r"><span id="A3.T10.3.5.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">+ <math id="A3.T10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{MIM}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{MIM}</annotation></semantics></math> + <math id="A3.T10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{obj}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>obj</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{obj}}</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq. <a href="#S3.E7" title="In 3.3 Learning Context via Object-Centric Objective ‣ 3 Learning Global Context with Object-Level Representation ‣ Context Matters: Learning Global Semantics for Visual Reasoning and Comprehension" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>)</span></td>
<td id="A3.T10.3.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="A3.T10.3.5.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">56.89</span></td></tr>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 10: </span>Effect of adding different loss terms in Eq. <a href="#S3.E7" title="In 3.3 Learning Context via Object-Centric Objective ‣ 3 Learning Global Context with Object-Level Representation ‣ Context Matters: Learning Global Semantics for Visual Reasoning and Comprehension" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> on VQA (v2.0). Combining both <math id="A3.T10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{MIM}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{MIM}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.T10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{obj}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>obj</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{obj}}</annotation></semantics></math> achieves the best performance.</figcaption>
</figure>
